==English==

===Phrase===
{{head|en|phrase|head=[[how]] [[do]] [[you]] [[like]] [[them]] [[apple]]s}}?

# {{context|colloquial|rhetorical question|lang=en}} directed [[jestingly]] or [[mockingly]] at someone who has received [[surprising]] information, [[ridicule|ridiculing]] the situation
#: ''"Our governor has just vetoed a bill that would offer more money to our schools. '''How do you like them apples'''?"''
# {{context|colloquial|rhetorical question|Irish|American|lang=en}} Used after an actual or proposed action with which the listener might be displeased. Also used after refuting an argument.
#: ''"I can't give you a raise now; if I did, this whole company would go bankrupt, and you wouldn't have a job at all. Now '''how do you like them apples'''?"'

Also,
"Jena Pothier ....  CAN NOT BE TRUSTED. SHE IS THE YELLOW EYED DEMON AND MUST DIE. THE ONLY THING THAT WOULD KILL HER IS THIS SPECIAL GUN..IT'S CALLED..THE COLT. "

